ublican environment could pull the margin back toward the state's underlying lean.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Illinois remains a Democratic-leaning state in presidential politics, with a partisan lean of about six points Democratic, and the 2028 race is fully open since the incumbent president is term-limited and neither party has settled on a nominee. No general-election polls or expert ratings are available for this race, so the outlook rests on the state's underlying partisan fundamentals.\n\nRecent signs point to continued Democratic strength. Governor JB Pritzker is widely mentioned as a 2028 presidential contender, has pledged $20 million to help midterm Democrats, and Democrats won statewide in 2026, including Juliana Stratton's victory. Those developments nudge the outlook slightly above the state's baseline lean, though the absence of polling keeps uncertainty wide. Illinois sits in Lean Democratic territory, with the Republican path running through a strong national environment.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7608, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.746, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7069, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7035, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7139, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7208, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7158, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.714, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7198, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.727, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7103, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.733, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.709, "margin": 6.0}, {"da